 "How do I act without clinging to the fruits of my actions?": {
  "answer": "Act because action is yours to do; the fruit is never yours to possess or control. Do not make yourself the “cause” of the result, and do not use non-attachment as an excuse for inaction. [gita 2.47]\n\n- Śaṅkara calls this yoga “skill”: samatva-buddhi (equanimous understanding) toward success and failure, while doing one’s own duty with the mind offered to Īśvara (the Lord). [gita 2.50]\n- The wise abandon the action-born fruit and are freed from the bondage of birth. [gita 2.51]\n- Desires may still appear, but they should dissolve without disturbing you or bringing you under their control. [gita 2.70]",
