 "What happens to the soul when the body dies?": {
  "answer": "When the body dies, Śaṅkara says the ātmā (self) is not killed or changed; the same changeless self attains another body [gita 2.30] [gita 2.13]. In his Īśā reading, the liṅga (subtle body), shaped by knowledge and action, departs, while the gross body ends as ash [isa 17].\n\n- After death, beings attain further births or worlds according to karma, even down to immobile forms [isa 3].\n- The wise person is not bewildered by this transition, because it is like passing through bodily states such as childhood, youth, and old age [gita 2.13].",
