 "How can a restless mind be made clear and steady?": {
  "answer": "Vyāsa’s answer is: cultivate the citta (mind) so it becomes prasanna (clear/serene); once clear, it becomes one-pointed and reaches steadiness [yogasutra 1.33]. Named supports include expelling and retaining the breath [yogasutra 1.34], making a particular object directly present in practice [yogasutra 1.35], and meditating on a chosen agreeable object [yogasutra 1.39].\n\n- The direct-object practice is meant to dispel doubt and let faith, energy, memory, and samādhi arise without obstruction [yogasutra 1.35].\n- Vyāsa assumes one enduring mind that can be distracted or gathered, not merely momentary cognitions [yogasutra 1.32].",
